          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The cited entry attests the whole modern term but does not document who coined it or when, so its origin remains unknown here. For memory only, the written form visibly contains आकाश, “sky,” and वाणी, “voice.” The one meaning to retrieve is “radio.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
